    {
      "type": "grammar",
      "title": "不要 + verb: don't …",
      "body": "To tell someone not to do something, put 不要 right before the verb. You can say it alone, like a command, or put 你 or 你们 in front to make it clear who you mean. It works like 'don't' in English.",
